---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, contactEmail } from "../data/site.js";

const title = "Privacy Policy | Count My Contractions";
const description =
  "Your contraction log stays in this browser. Count My Contractions does not collect accounts or analytics. Advertising cookies may be added later.";
const path = "/privacy";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: "Contraction timer", path: "/" }, { name: "Privacy", path }])]}
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Timer</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Privacy</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated October 5, 2026.</p>
    <p>
      Count My Contractions is a static website. This policy explains what the site stores today and what could change if advertising is added later. It is written in plain language so you can use the timer without hunting through legalese.
    </p>

    <h2>The contraction log stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      When you time a contraction, the start time, end time, and the pattern you selected (5-1-1, 4-1-1, or 3-1-1) are saved in your browser with localStorage. A short undo history is saved the same way. Theme choice, light or dark, is also stored locally. None of that information is sent to Count My Contractions, because there is no account system, no database, and no contraction-log server.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anyone who can unlock your phone and open this site in the same browser can see the log. If you share a device, clear the session when you are done, or use a private window knowing that some private windows discard storage when they close. To remove the log yourself, use Clear session on the timer, then Undo only if you did that by mistake. You can also clear site data or local storage for countmycontractions.com in your browser settings. Uninstalling a home-screen shortcut does not always erase browser storage; clearing site data does.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>
      This version of the site does not use analytics, advertising pixels, or a cookie banner, because it does not set tracking cookies. It does not ask for your name, email, due date, location, or medical history. The contact address is an email you choose to write. If you email us, we will see whatever you put in that message, including the address you send from. Please do not send medical records or a copy of your contraction log unless you mean to.
    </p>
    <p>
      Server logs may exist at the host that delivers the pages. On Vercel, that can include routine technical data such as IP address, browser type, and the page requested, kept by the host under its own policy for security and operations. We do not use those logs to build a profile, and we do not sell them. We do not sell personal information because we do not operate an account database to sell.
    </p>

    <h2>Offline copies on your device</h2>
    <p>
      After a first visit, a service worker may cache the pages, styles, and the printable PDF so the timer can open without a network. That cache is on your device. It is not a copy of your contraction log on our side. Updating the site replaces the old cache when you are next online.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising that may be added later</h2>
    <p>
      The site may later show ads through Google AdSense so it can remain free. If that happens, Google and its partners may set cookies or use similar technologies to serve and measure ads, including ads based on your activity on other sites, depending on your Google ad settings and local law. Those technologies are not active in this version. Before any AdSense code is added, this policy will be updated to describe it, and the site will follow Google's consent requirements where they apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reserved boxes labeled "Advertisement" are empty placeholders. They do not contact an ad network. You will be able to see the difference because a real unit would display an ad, not a sentence saying nothing is loaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google's own description of how it uses information from sites and apps that use its services is at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
      Ad personalization controls are in your Google account, where those controls are available.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The site is for adults timing labor, and for adults supporting them. It is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top will change and the new version will be posted on this page. Continued use of the site after an update means you are using it under the posted policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy can go to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. That address is a placeholder until the owner connects a real mailbox. Do not use it for urgent medical help.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
